WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:11.600
Ah. Hm.

2
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.533
Hmm.

3
00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:21.900
Yeah, come in.

4
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.799
- Are you going out?
- Hey, Mom.

5
00:00:26.799 --> 00:00:30.966
- Which one should I wear?
- Hmm. I'd go with that!

6
00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.900
Mm? OK. This one!

7
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.366
Fletch! Fletch!

8
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:38.199
If you already knew, why did you ask?

9
00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:41.699
Whichever one you didn't pick is the cuter one, that's why!

10
00:00:41.766 --> 00:00:45.866
I see. So. Where are you going?

11
00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:50.333
Lumiose City! To see Professor Sycamore and get my very first Pokémon!

12
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.500
♪ I want to be the very best Like no one ever was ♪

13
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.266
♪ To catch them is my real test

14
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

15
00:01:04.366 --> 00:01:07.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

16
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:10.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

17
00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:14.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

18
00:01:14.066 --> 00:01:16.433
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

19
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

20
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

21
00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:34.000
In Lumiose City, Ash has just befriended Froakie,

22
00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.433
his first Kalos region Pokémon, at Professor Sycamore's research lab.

23
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.500
Come on, hurry it up, you two!

24
00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:44.333
Ash, you can register for the Kalos League over this way!

25
00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:47.766
- Yeah, we know, Bonnie.
- There's no need to rush.

26
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:50.066
The Pokémon Center will still be there.

27
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:53.800
Thanks a lot, Clemont. It's nice of you to bring me here.

28
00:01:53.866 --> 00:01:58.266
Please, think nothing of it, Ash. I confess I'm a little in awe of you.

29
00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.666
- In awe?
- You were willing to do anything

30
00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:04.233
you could to help Pikachu and that Garchomp back there.

31
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.800
- Just watching you gave me courage.
- Oh, come on.

32
00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:10.633
- It wasn't that big of a deal.
- It was.

33
00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:13.700
I can totally understand why Froakie chose you.

34
00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.733
-Hmm.

35
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:23.633
I'll just have to do better.

36
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.633
- Huh?
- Sorry. Just talking to myself.

37
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.133
Wow.

38
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.700
- Good morning.
- Good morning to you, Nurse Joy.

39
00:02:39.766 --> 00:02:41.200
At this Pokémon Center,

40
00:02:41.266 --> 00:02:43.866
helping Pokémon in need is our number one goal!

41
00:02:43.933 --> 00:02:46.700
We're here for Trainers and Pokémon alike.

42
00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.433
I was hoping you could help me register for the Kalos League.

43
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.433
I sure can! If you please, touch this panel with your Pokédex.

44
00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.900
Okay.

45
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.966
Ash from Pallet Town is now registered

46
00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.433
to enter the Kalos League.

47
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.299
Number of badges currently in your possession, zero.

48
00:03:05.366 --> 00:03:07.000
We wish you the best of luck.

49
00:03:07.066 --> 00:03:09.633
- Hm.
- You're all set now, Ash!

50
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.233
Awesome! And I'm going to win!

51
00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:15.000
My next step in becoming a Pokémon Master!

52
00:03:15.066 --> 00:03:19.733
And every registered Trainer is eligible to receive a Kalos region badge case here!

53
00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.633
Wigglytuff.

54
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.733
- A Wigglytuff!
- Pika!

55
00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:26.799
Why, yes! Here in the Kalos region,

56
00:03:26.866 --> 00:03:29.966
my able Pokémon Center assistant is Wigglytuff.

57
00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:33.166
That's great. Thanks, Wigglytuff!

58
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:35.066
Wigglytuff!

59
00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:39.233
You're all registered. Good luck, train hard and always do your best!

60
00:03:39.299 --> 00:03:40.633
Right!

61
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.633
- Count on it!
- Pika!

62
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.600
Good news, Boss.

63
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:55.866
We arrived in the Kalos region on time and according to plan.

64
00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:59.600
Our goal is to catch as many rare and powerful Pokémon as possible.

65
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:04.666
And we're totally committed to that goal. You can count on us.

66
00:04:04.733 --> 00:04:06.666
- Good.

67
00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:11.399
I'm certain the Pokémon you catch will be an important addition to our work.

68
00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:14.399
- Get to it.
- Sir!

69
00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:19.666
Yes! The Boss said for us to get to it!

70
00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:21.466
He's counting on us. Yipee-yay!

71
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:24.400
We're the first step in Team Rocket's takeover of Kalos,

72
00:04:24.466 --> 00:04:26.766
'cause no one does takeovers like we do!

73
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.500
Huh? My croissant.

74
00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:37.433
- Hey, Rotom!
- Pika!

75
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.500
Rotom!

76
00:04:39.566 --> 00:04:43.566
- Hello, Ash! How are things so far?
- Great.

77
00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:47.433
We arrived safely in Kalos region. We're starting our journey soon!

78
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.866
- Good! Have fun on the road.
- Thanks!

79
00:04:50.933 --> 00:04:53.466
I already got my first Kalos Pokémon!

80
00:04:53.533 --> 00:04:56.099
- Wonderful!
- Check it out!

81
00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.599
Ah! What have we here? A Froakie! A Kalos Water-type Pokémon!

82
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:05.866
You're right. You know everything.

83
00:05:05.933 --> 00:05:09.300
-Hey, Rotom! I can't see! Move!

84
00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:22.066
- Guys! Thanks for waiting!
- Huh? Hi, Ash.

85
00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.800
Didn't you tell us you were going to challenge the Santalune Gym first?

86
00:05:25.866 --> 00:05:29.599
Yeah. I'm pretty sure the Gym Leader should be back by now.

87
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:32.566
I think the best way to get to Santalune City

88
00:05:32.633 --> 00:05:36.599
is by traveling Route 4 all the way there.

89
00:05:36.666 --> 00:05:38.500
Then Route 4 it is!

90
00:05:38.566 --> 00:05:41.333
- Aren't you psyched, Pikachu?
- Pika!

91
00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.099
- Froakie, you're going to be great.
- Froakie!

92
00:05:44.166 --> 00:05:47.599
- So why don't we hit the road?
- Let's go!

93
00:05:47.666 --> 00:05:50.266
The sooner we leave, the sooner we're there.

94
00:05:50.333 --> 00:05:52.333
You don't have to show me around anymore.

95
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:56.500
Silly Ash! We're all really, really good friends now, right?

96
00:05:56.566 --> 00:05:59.099
- So we're going with you!
- No joke?

97
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:01.400
- Pika?
- We're serious.

98
00:06:01.466 --> 00:06:03.633
Remember what you did back there?

99
00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.400
You showed me what it's like to have real courage

100
00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:10.800
I know I can get stronger. We both can get stronger traveling with you.

101
00:06:10.866 --> 00:06:15.200
- You're right, Clemont.
- Mm. So that okay?

102
00:06:15.266 --> 00:06:18.933
Of course it's OK. Traveling with friends is way more fun.

103
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.433
All right, it's a deal. We'll have a great time!

104
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.433
Yeah. We sure will.

105
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.500
Hey! No fair. I can't reach!

106
00:06:30.566 --> 00:06:34.233
Let's go meet lots and lots of Pokémon!

107
00:06:34.299 --> 00:06:38.933
Right! Good friends, together! Kalos, here we come!

108
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.299
Yeah!

109
00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.799
-Rhyhorn!

110
00:06:47.866 --> 00:06:51.233
Got to go. Wish me luck.

111
00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:54.766
So, do you know which Pokémon you want?

112
00:06:54.833 --> 00:06:56.500
- Uh-huh.
- Which one?

113
00:06:56.566 --> 00:06:59.099
It's a secret!

114
00:06:59.166 --> 00:07:01.333
Hmm.

115
00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.066
I'm off. Later!

116
00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:04.633
Bye. Take care!

117
00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:09.299
Don't forget to practice your Rhyhorn Racing!

118
00:07:09.366 --> 00:07:11.666
I won't. Bye!

119
00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:17.200
I guess we'll just see about that.

120
00:07:29.966 --> 00:07:31.466
Hey, what's up, you two?

121
00:07:33.533 --> 00:07:35.466
- Huh?
- Pika.

122
00:07:40.666 --> 00:07:44.033
- Huh?
- Pika? Pik, pik.

123
00:07:44.099 --> 00:07:46.200
Pi... Pika?

124
00:07:46.266 --> 00:07:49.599
- What was that?
- Bonnie, are you okay?

125
00:07:49.666 --> 00:07:52.200
- Wow, that was a shock!
- What was it?

126
00:07:52.266 --> 00:07:54.200
Huh?

127
00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:56.833
Hm. Maybe it wanted this.

128
00:07:58.766 --> 00:08:01.133
- Huh? Huh?
- Pika!

129
00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.200
- Never seen that Pokémon.
- Na-na!

130
00:08:04.266 --> 00:08:07.299
It's so cute!

131
00:08:07.366 --> 00:08:09.333
Na-na-na.

132
00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.266
Dedenne!

133
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:12.500
Pika pika!

134
00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.000
It sure doesn't look like it's afraid of us.

135
00:08:17.066 --> 00:08:20.200
They're Electric types, so they communicate with electricity.

136
00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.000
Oh, so that's an Electric type?

137
00:08:23.566 --> 00:08:26.099
Dedenne. The Antenna Pokémon.

138
00:08:26.166 --> 00:08:28.766
Dedenne communicates long distance with other Dedenne

139
00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:31.733
by sending radio waves through its antenna-like whiskers.

140
00:08:31.799 --> 00:08:34.466
Wow. So that's a Dedenne!

141
00:08:34.533 --> 00:08:37.966
I want it so bad! Hey! You'll keep it for me, won't you?

142
00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.666
- Keep it?
- Yeah.

143
00:08:39.733 --> 00:08:42.600
He'll keep it for me until I'm old enough to become a Trainer.

144
00:08:42.666 --> 00:08:46.000
Pretty, pretty please! I promise I'll take care of it.

145
00:08:46.066 --> 00:08:48.600
Hmm. Let me see.

146
00:08:48.666 --> 00:08:51.833
Aw, do it. I can help you catch it, if you want.

147
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.199
You will? Thanks a lot, Ash!

148
00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:56.733
All right, then. Let's catch Dedenne.

149
00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.466
Hmm. Huh? Right!

150
00:08:59.533 --> 00:09:04.000
Hey, Dedenne. You wanted this, right?

151
00:09:04.066 --> 00:09:06.733
It must have thought Pikachu was going to take it.

152
00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.933
- Hm. That's right. Here, take it.
- Pika.

153
00:09:15.366 --> 00:09:20.333
Hey, what's the big idea? I've never seen that Pokémon either.

154
00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:23.199
- It's a Fletchling.
- No fair!

155
00:09:23.266 --> 00:09:26.199
That berry belongs to Dedenne!

156
00:09:26.266 --> 00:09:29.633
Fletch! Fletch! Fletchling!

157
00:09:29.699 --> 00:09:32.066
-Fletchling ate the berry.

158
00:09:33.566 --> 00:09:36.266
Fletchling, the Tiny Robin Pokémon.

159
00:09:36.333 --> 00:09:39.066
Although Fletchling's chirp is quite beautiful to hear,

160
00:09:39.133 --> 00:09:42.933
it is relentlessly tough with those who enter its territory.

161
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.733
-Pika?

162
00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.233
- Froakie.
- Dedenne, what's the matter?

163
00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.466
Dedenne!

164
00:09:51.533 --> 00:09:53.666
-Dedenne, wait!

165
00:09:55.733 --> 00:09:57.900
I don't think it's going to come back.

166
00:09:57.966 --> 00:09:59.833
-Fro?

167
00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:03.233
- Froakie!
- Fletch! Fletch! Fletch!

168
00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.699
It dodged all of that.

169
00:10:05.766 --> 00:10:09.266
Look at that. Fletchling's fast.

170
00:10:09.333 --> 00:10:13.199
All right! I'm going to catch that Fletchling now!

171
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.000
Fletchling!

172
00:10:17.066 --> 00:10:19.533
Who's that Pokémon?

173
00:10:24.066 --> 00:10:26.199
It's Fletchling!

174
00:10:30.066 --> 00:10:31.866
Fletchling's a Flying type.

175
00:10:31.933 --> 00:10:34.266
Pikachu has the advantage, as an Electric type.

176
00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:37.266
-Froakie!

177
00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:40.133
- Hey, Pikachu, let's go!
- Pika!

178
00:10:40.199 --> 00:10:43.333
- Froakie!
- Pika?

179
00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.400
- Froakie!
- Fletch! Fletch! Fletchling!

180
00:10:46.466 --> 00:10:49.600
Come on, Froakie! We don't even have a plan.

181
00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:55.000
- Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.
- Pikachu! Pi... Ka...

182
00:10:55.066 --> 00:10:57.933
- Fro! Fro!
- Pika!

183
00:10:59.566 --> 00:11:01.300
It's using Double Team!

184
00:11:04.933 --> 00:11:08.600
Fletchling!

185
00:11:11.533 --> 00:11:13.533
Froakie!

186
00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.600
Froakie, are you okay?

187
00:11:15.666 --> 00:11:18.533
Take it easy. Just let Pikachu handle this.

188
00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.533
Pika pika!

189
00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:22.233
- Froakie.
- Huh?

190
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.733
Huh?

191
00:11:25.366 --> 00:11:30.533
- Ah! Wait!
- Fro! Fro! Froakie!

192
00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.066
-Wait, Froakie!

193
00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:36.800
Hold on. Didn't Professor Sycamore say that Froakie had a habit

194
00:11:36.866 --> 00:11:39.166
of ignoring its Trainer when battling?

195
00:11:39.233 --> 00:11:41.233
- I'm starting to understand.
- Huh?

196
00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.966
Stories about Froakie leaving its Trainers? I get it.

197
00:11:45.033 --> 00:11:47.133
- Huh?
- Pika?

198
00:11:49.533 --> 00:11:52.900
Ah, my kingdom for a little bit of breakfast.

199
00:11:52.966 --> 00:11:54.666
My departed croissant!

200
00:11:54.733 --> 00:11:58.100
It may be a bit early for lunch, but let's bend the rules.

201
00:11:58.166 --> 00:12:00.233
Wow! I second that.

202
00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.699
Come back, sandwich! Ah! Oh!

203
00:12:06.766 --> 00:12:10.466
Huh? Did you just see what I saw?

204
00:12:10.533 --> 00:12:14.033
- Something with a touch of white.
- A Pokémon, I'll bet.

205
00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.633
Wobbuffet!

206
00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.400
Huh?

207
00:12:21.466 --> 00:12:23.633
Wobbuffet!

208
00:12:27.766 --> 00:12:31.433
-Stop, Froakie! Just chill out!

209
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.600
You're only going to end up hurting yourself.

210
00:12:33.666 --> 00:12:36.366
- Fro! Froakie!
- I know how you feel, Froakie.

211
00:12:36.433 --> 00:12:39.766
- But you've got to listen to me.
- Ash!

212
00:12:44.466 --> 00:12:47.466
- Everybody okay?
- Fro?

213
00:12:47.533 --> 00:12:52.533
Pikachu? Froakie? Clemont and Bonnie, are you guys okay too?

214
00:12:52.599 --> 00:12:55.633
- Yeah, Ash, we're all right.
- Pika.

215
00:12:55.699 --> 00:12:57.766
Hey, Froakie? I understand.

216
00:12:57.833 --> 00:13:01.266
You wanted to get even with Fletchling for making Bonnie sad.

217
00:13:01.333 --> 00:13:03.233
Froak.

218
00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.066
Is that true? Thank you, Froakie!

219
00:13:06.133 --> 00:13:08.066
-Froakie!

220
00:13:08.133 --> 00:13:09.533
Fletchling!

221
00:13:09.599 --> 00:13:12.566
But you can't do that without a plan.

222
00:13:12.633 --> 00:13:15.099
Okay, Fletchling can fly.

223
00:13:15.166 --> 00:13:18.066
So first we need to figure out a way to lure it in.

224
00:13:18.133 --> 00:13:22.233
Well, you just leave it to me!

225
00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:27.566
You see, the future is now, thanks to science! Clemontic Gear on!

226
00:13:27.633 --> 00:13:31.000
Presenting my Flying-type Pokémon Attractor Machine!

227
00:13:32.066 --> 00:13:36.166
- Ah!
- The name could use a little work.

228
00:13:36.233 --> 00:13:39.133
You see, Bird Pokémon have a homing instinct.

229
00:13:39.199 --> 00:13:41.900
By using sound waves of a certain frequency,

230
00:13:41.966 --> 00:13:45.233
this little invention of mine can attract or repel Bird Pokémon

231
00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:49.733
by affecting their internal compass. Watch this. Power on!

232
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.533
Fletch. Fletchling.

233
00:13:55.599 --> 00:14:00.866
- It's starting to work.
- So cool. Man, science is the amazing!

234
00:14:00.933 --> 00:14:03.833
- Huh?
- Fletchling!

235
00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.533
I don't understand.

236
00:14:05.599 --> 00:14:07.333
- Pika?
- Fro?

237
00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.400
- It makes no sense.
- Huh?

238
00:14:09.466 --> 00:14:12.333
- Hey, Clemont?
- Something's staring at us.

239
00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.933
- Beedrill!
- Pika!

240
00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.833
- They were attracted by it?
- Turn off the machine!

241
00:14:21.133 --> 00:14:25.566
-They're coming after us. Let's go!

242
00:14:25.633 --> 00:14:27.933
I must have picked too low a frequency

243
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:32.099
when a higher frequency would have worked a whole lot better on Bird Pokémon!

244
00:14:32.166 --> 00:14:34.133
Let's try this!

245
00:14:34.199 --> 00:14:38.133
Stop it, Clemont! You're making the Beedrill even angrier than before!

246
00:14:38.199 --> 00:14:40.666
I'm sure I can affect the Flying-type Pokémon

247
00:14:40.733 --> 00:14:44.333
if I just crank it up full blast. Here goes!

248
00:14:53.699 --> 00:14:58.566
- Looks like you blew it again.
- Huh? The Beedrill are flying away.

249
00:14:58.633 --> 00:15:01.233
We're fine now. Is everybody okay?

250
00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.166
- Yeah, I'm fine.
- But why?

251
00:15:04.233 --> 00:15:07.733
Clemont, that was great. You attracted all those Beedrill!

252
00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.099
Huh. I guess I did.

253
00:15:10.166 --> 00:15:11.533
- Fletch! Fletchling!
- Huh?

254
00:15:15.366 --> 00:15:17.133
Hey, it's laughing at us.

255
00:15:19.199 --> 00:15:23.366
Huh? I just got an idea.

256
00:15:25.966 --> 00:15:28.266
That's a new Pokémon on me.

257
00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.833
- Huh. Inkay.
- Huh?

258
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.199
No. Not huh. That's its name.

259
00:15:35.266 --> 00:15:36.766
Wobbuffet!

260
00:15:36.833 --> 00:15:39.366
Whatever its name, let's make it ours!

261
00:15:39.433 --> 00:15:43.266
- Inkay? Okay!
- Then we'll just have to battle it.

262
00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:45.066
Take it away, Wobbuffet.

263
00:15:45.133 --> 00:15:47.133
Inkay!

264
00:15:47.199 --> 00:15:50.000
- Wah!
- Now, that's what I call quick.

265
00:15:50.066 --> 00:15:53.766
All right, smarty pants. Feast your eyes on these!

266
00:15:53.833 --> 00:15:56.366
- Inkay!
- Our lunch!

267
00:15:56.433 --> 00:15:58.500
I thought you were starving.

268
00:15:58.566 --> 00:16:01.066
Inkay took the bait. Watch this!

269
00:16:01.133 --> 00:16:02.699
Huh?

270
00:16:09.699 --> 00:16:11.866
I caught an Inkay!

271
00:16:11.933 --> 00:16:15.333
Fletch! Fletch!

272
00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.266
This is it, the perfect place to battle.

273
00:16:18.333 --> 00:16:20.333
Time to settle the score.

274
00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:21.433
- Fro?
- Pika?

275
00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.066
Settle the score?

276
00:16:23.133 --> 00:16:25.966
He means he's going to catch Fletchling.

277
00:16:26.033 --> 00:16:29.000
Yup. Together. I'm your Trainer, right?

278
00:16:29.066 --> 00:16:31.533
- That means it's you and me.
- Froakie.

279
00:16:31.599 --> 00:16:35.066
Great. This whole area will be the battlefield.

280
00:16:35.133 --> 00:16:39.466
It's full of high and low places and with your awesome jumping skills, you'll rock.

281
00:16:39.533 --> 00:16:42.533
-I have no idea what any of that meant.

282
00:16:42.599 --> 00:16:47.099
Go, Froakie! Jump above Fletchling. Ready?

283
00:16:47.166 --> 00:16:50.133
Fro! Fro! Fro! Fro!

284
00:16:50.199 --> 00:16:52.000
Yes! Now, jump higher!

285
00:16:52.066 --> 00:16:55.033
Ash is taking advantage of all the different ledge heights

286
00:16:55.099 --> 00:16:58.033
and, combined with those amazing jumping skills,

287
00:16:58.099 --> 00:17:01.000
Froakie will have even more mobility.

288
00:17:01.066 --> 00:17:03.199
- Fletch! Fletchling!
- Fro! Fro!

289
00:17:03.266 --> 00:17:04.966
Now! Use Water Pulse!

290
00:17:05.033 --> 00:17:09.366
-Froakie! Fro!

291
00:17:09.433 --> 00:17:14.133
- Make it hard to fly!
- Froakie!

292
00:17:22.033 --> 00:17:23.366
Fletchling!

293
00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.500
- It's a decoy!
- Great, Froakie!

294
00:17:31.566 --> 00:17:34.700
Now. Bubble, go!

295
00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.366
Fletchling!

296
00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:41.100
All right! Go, Poké Ball.

297
00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.866
-Fletchling!

298
00:17:49.933 --> 00:17:52.733
- No, it didn't work!
- You were so close.

299
00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:58.300
It's attacking! Jump up and get above it again!

300
00:17:58.366 --> 00:18:02.533
Fro! Fro!

301
00:18:03.666 --> 00:18:06.800
- Water Pulse!
- Froakie!

302
00:18:06.866 --> 00:18:09.333
Fletchling!

303
00:18:13.033 --> 00:18:15.233
This time for sure.

304
00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:17.466
Go, Poké Ball!

305
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Yeah!

306
00:18:29.399 --> 00:18:31.166
-Fro!

307
00:18:33.866 --> 00:18:37.166
I caught... a Fletchling!

308
00:18:40.399 --> 00:18:41.899
Fro!

309
00:18:41.966 --> 00:18:46.933
You okay, Froakie? I caught Fletchling 'cause of you.

310
00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.633
-Pika, pika!

311
00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:51.300
- Wasn't that amazing?
- Sure was!

312
00:18:51.366 --> 00:18:53.666
Froakie's jumping kept getting better.

313
00:18:53.733 --> 00:18:55.366
Same with your teamwork.

314
00:18:55.433 --> 00:18:59.533
Yeah. I'm starting to understand a lot about Froakie. Thanks.

315
00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:01.200
- Pika, pika!
- Froak.

316
00:19:01.266 --> 00:19:03.966
Come on out, Fletchling!

317
00:19:04.033 --> 00:19:06.200
Fletch! Fletchling!

318
00:19:06.266 --> 00:19:10.133
From now on, we're going to be good friends, all of us!

319
00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:13.700
And, Fletchling, tell me if you get hungry next time,

320
00:19:13.766 --> 00:19:16.899
because stealing other Pokémon's food is bad.

321
00:19:16.966 --> 00:19:20.100
- Fletchling!
- Okay. You're forgiven.

322
00:19:20.166 --> 00:19:23.366
How about an Oran Berry to celebrate our new friendship?

323
00:19:23.433 --> 00:19:25.533
You too, Pikachu and Froakie.

324
00:19:30.066 --> 00:19:33.866
Great! All right! Let's all head to the Santalune Gym!

325
00:19:33.933 --> 00:19:37.433
And so Ash has another new friend, Fletchling.

326
00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:41.266
Now, as Ash, Clemont and Bonnie set their sights on Santalune City,

327
00:19:41.333 --> 00:19:44.366
our heroes' journey truly begins.

328
00:19:46.666 --> 00:19:50.333
Hello? Is Professor Sycamore around?

329
00:19:50.399 --> 00:19:52.566
That’s me. I’m up here.

330
00:19:52.633 --> 00:19:55.566
Huh? Hello there. I’m Serena.

331
00:19:55.633 --> 00:19:58.633
I’ll bet you’re here to become a Pokémon Trainer.

332
00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:02.899
Yup. Also, Professor, I saw this Trainer on the news.

333
00:20:02.966 --> 00:20:06.133
The report was all about how he had saved a Garchomp.

334
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.333
Oh, you're talking about Ash.

335
00:20:08.399 --> 00:20:10.866
Ash? I knew it!

336
00:20:10.933 --> 00:20:13.100
I’m afraid that he already left.

337
00:20:13.166 --> 00:20:15.866
He says that he was going to challenge the Santalune Gym.

338
00:20:15.933 --> 00:20:18.466
Santalune Gym? Hmm.

339
00:20:18.533 --> 00:20:20.866
Professor, may I choose a Pokémon?

340
00:20:20.933 --> 00:20:24.966
Of course. And do you have any idea which Pokémon you'd like?

341
00:20:25.033 --> 00:20:27.866
- Yup.
- All right. Everybody out!

342
00:20:33.033 --> 00:20:34.766
These are the Kalos Pokémon

343
00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:38.933
new Trainers may choose from, Fennekin, Chespin and Froakie.

344
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:42.100
Which Pokémon will you choose as your partner?
